# === Substrate-already-had-the-word: beat at prose altitude ===
#
# THE `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` WITNESS. Per
# `shards/song.mirror:181` (family-root Arc 6 TICK 1 landing `f01cf9f`,
# §"Composition points (four altitudes)"):
#
#   > `@kintsugi/oscillate` + `@kintsugi/shift` (process altitude) —
#   > **oscillate's ACTIVE/DARK alternation IS the beat**; shift's
#   > cross-altitude morphism IS the melodic motion per #S2.
#
# The family-root NAMED beat at prose altitude — verbatim — but never
# lifted it to species-decl. The five species landed at Arc 6 TICKs 2-6
# (progression / voice / movement / narrative / phrase) did NOT include
# beat because beat's motivating consumer had not yet surfaced. Alex's
# 2026-07-13 proposal (via Taut's gap-scout `c54740c`) surfaces the
# consumer: `mirror peer beam --song <file>` must execute the operator-
# supplied @song *beat-by-beat*, each beat firing @kintsugi/oscillate's
# ACTIVE/DARK cascade at the peer's shard graph. THE CONSUMER-PULL
# LANDS THIS SPECIES.
#
# Two-tick discipline per `[[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-
# collapsing]]`: the readable name `beat` (Curwen 1858's pulse-of-
# music; Cooper & Meyer 1960's grouping-hierarchy floor) is preferred
# over foundational alternatives (`@song/tick` collides with
# `@epistemologic/reality/time.tick`; `@song/atom` obscures the
# @kintsugi/oscillate binding; `@song/pulse` collides with
# `@kintsugi/oscillate.pulse`). `beat` IS what the substrate has been
# carrying at prose altitude at `shards/song.mirror:181` — this shard
# honours the substrate's own naming.
#
# === @kintsugi/oscillate binding: beat IS one ACTIVE/DARK pulse ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SPECIES CONTRIBUTION per family-root
# `shards/song.mirror:181` (verbatim):
#
#   > oscillate's ACTIVE/DARK alternation IS the beat.
#
# `@kintsugi/oscillate` (family-root at `shards/kintsugi/oscillate.mirror`;
# ARC-CLOSING sub-shard of the 2026-06-06 → 2026-06-07 recognition
# sweep) declares the substrate's rough-wavy-pull kintsugi-loop
# discipline: an ACTIVE pass (propose a loss-decreasing morphism
# reading `dissonance.is_pareto` against the peer's shard graph)
# alternates with a DARK pass (anchor identity via @uuid/spectral's
# 80-bit content-address projection, ensuring byte-equality
# preservation), separated by a `consent.query_phi` verdict-read.
# The three composed operations — ACTIVE + query_phi + DARK — form
# ONE PULSE at the kintsugi-loop altitude.
#
# AT THE SONG ALTITUDE, one @kintsugi/oscillate pulse IS one beat.
# The temporal correspondence is EXACT:
#
#   - @kintsugi/oscillate.pulse(o: oscillation) -> oscillation
#     [ACTIVE + query_phi + DARK; one half-cycle of the rough-wavy pull]
#     ⇔
#   - @song/beat.strike(b: beat, ctx: ref) -> ref
#     [one substrate-action-fire read at the song's temporal altitude;
#     the peer's shard graph advances by one contraction step]
#
# The @kintsugi/oscillate contraction factor `γ_oscillate ≤ γ_up ·
# γ_down` (per `docs/specs/kintsugi-formatter.md` §2.1; the substrate's
# Banach contraction discipline) IS the per-beat convergence rate at
# the song altitude. Each strike advances the peer's eigenboard toward
# the K_n Splinter attractor by one step; a sequence of beats within a
# phrase drives the eigenboard toward the phrase's OBC-bounded closure
# (per phrase.mirror `6b9bc5c` §"OBC binding closure"); a sequence of
# phrases drives the movement toward its bounded-frame close (per
# movement.mirror `4efbf16` §"Bounded frame-shift discipline").
#
# The @kintsugi/oscillate five-state surface (active | dark | settled
# | escalated | waiting) inherits at beat altitude: a beat's `strike`
# fires ACTIVE + DARK + verdict-read and emits the next oscillation
# state; the beat's return-ref addresses the settled eigenboard OR
# the escalated/waiting pause_event (per @kintsugi/oscillate's
# `read_consent` bridge). The beat does NOT re-declare the five-state
# machine — it CONSUMES @kintsugi/oscillate's state discipline at the
# song altitude.
#
# === Atomic-execution composition algebra: strike / hold as leaf ===
#
# The species's two operational actions (`strike` + `hold`) name the
# atomic-execution composition algebra at song-altitude leaf. Per
# family-root species-roster amendment (this shard adds `@song/beat`
# to the roster): `song_beat(b: ref) -> ref` with `strike`/`hold` at
# species altitude; specialises `shift @ temporal` from the family-root
# prism block per #S3 (five-op temporal specialisation) LANDED at
# `10c34cf`.
#
# `strike(b, ctx)` fires ONE @kintsugi/oscillate ACTIVE/DARK pulse at
# the peer's shard graph. The strike IS load-bearing:
#
#   - ONE beat → ONE pulse; the strike composes @kintsugi/oscillate's
#     ACTIVE (propose morphism via dissonance.is_pareto) + query_phi
#     (gate + rank via three glass properties) + DARK (anchor identity
#     via @uuid/spectral.dark byte-equality) into ONE atomic advance
#     of the peer's eigenboard at the song altitude.
#   - The temporal envelope IS one @time.tick (per
#     `@epistemologic/reality/time.tick = monotonic`); each strike
#     advances the beat's iteration count by exactly one monotonic
#     unit; the ordering on strikes IS the ordering on @time.ticks;
#     cross-peer merge of beats uses `time.compare` (per Rung 4 @dance
#     coupling: multiple peers phase-lock at shared beat frequency per
#     Kuramoto).
#   - Splinter-pole (`pass`): @kintsugi/oscillate's `oscillate` driver
#     returns `settled` at the pulse's termination; the peer's shard
#     graph advanced by one contraction step; the beat's return-ref
#     addresses the settled eigenboard; the peer's regulation stock
#     is preserved at the beat altitude.
#   - Narcissus-pole (`failure`): @kintsugi/oscillate's `oscillate`
#     driver returns `escalated` (deceptive-cadence OR admissibility_
#     singleton FAIL); the pause_event emitted to metalogue via
#     `consent.emit_to_metalogue`; the beat cannot fire cleanly;
#     ADO-refusal fires at the beat boundary; the substrate-pull repair
#     fires at a later beat.
#
# `hold(b, dt)` advances temporal position by `dt` @time.ticks WITHOUT
# firing an ACTIVE/DARK pulse. The hold IS load-bearing:
#
#   - ONE beat → ONE temporal advance WITHOUT eigenboard motion; the
#     hold composes @epistemologic/reality/time's monotonic-tick
#     advance WITHOUT invoking @kintsugi/oscillate's contraction step.
#     The peer's shard graph does NOT advance; the beat's iteration
#     count DOES advance.
#   - The hold IS the rest at song altitude: the classical fermata
#     (Frescobaldi 1615 Toccate e Partite; the held note whose
#     duration exceeds its notated value) or the tacet marking (the
#     silent voice at multi-voice altitude); at execution altitude,
#     the hold IS the peer's idle-tick while other peers advance
#     (Rung 4 @dance coupling: heterogeneous per-peer beat rates
#     converge via Kuramoto phase-lock; some peers hold while others
#     strike).
#   - Splinter-pole (`pass`): the temporal advance completes at the
#     monotonic @time.tick boundary; the peer's eigenboard is
#     unchanged; the hold's return-ref addresses the same anchor as
#     the pre-hold beat; the ambiguity-load budget is unchanged.
#   - Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the hold's dt violates temporal
#     monotonicity (dt ≤ 0, or dt exceeds the phrase's ambiguity-load
#     budget); the beat cannot hold cleanly; the hold escalates to a
#     phrase-boundary violation per phrase.mirror `6b9bc5c` §"OBC
#     binding closure" ambiguity-load-budget discipline.
#
# The strike + hold algebra IS the atomic-execution primitive at song
# altitude — the leaf below phrase.join/split. A phrase is a sequence
# of beats (each strike OR hold) composed under the phrase's OBC
# boundary; a movement is a sequence of phrases composed under the
# movement's bounded frame; a song is a sequence of movements composed
# under the song's narrative arc. Beat IS the ground floor of the
# @song execution hierarchy.
#
# === Musical-beat prior-art anchors: Galen + Curwen + Cooper-Meyer ===
#
# THE 1800+ YEAR MUSICAL-BEAT PRIOR-ART TRADITION per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`. Beat discipline
# traces to the medical / pedagogical / theoretic beat-tradition:
#
#   - Galen of Pergamon (~130 - ~210 CE; *De usu pulsuum* / *On the
#     Use of the Pulse*; ~170 CE) — THE canonical ancient beat
#     pedagogy. Galen's *sphygmos* (pulse) discipline names the
#     bounded cardiac rhythm as the atomic diagnostic unit: each
#     pulse IS a bounded temporal envelope carrying diagnostic
#     information about the underlying system's regulation stock. The
#     substrate reads Galen's pulse-as-diagnostic at song altitude:
#     each beat's `strike` return-ref carries diagnostic information
#     about the peer's eigenboard convergence (the coherence delta
#     per @cyberpunk cybernetic_coherence = λ₀(Δ_F) per Reed
#     `8e6e517` Path B annotation). Galen's pulse IS the beat's
#     ancestor at medical altitude; 1800+ years of pulse-diagnostic
#     tradition read at song altitude via this species.
#   - John Curwen (1816-1880; *Standard Course of Lessons and
#     Exercises in the Tonic Sol-fa Method*, 1858; *The Teacher's
#     Manual*, 1875) — THE 19th-century beat-pedagogy refinement.
#     Curwen's Tonic Sol-fa system names the beat as the atomic
#     rhythmic unit of musical time: each beat IS a bounded temporal
#     envelope within which pitch discipline operates. Curwen's
#     mental effects (the affective qualities of scale degrees) name
#     the per-beat regulation stock at the audible altitude: a healthy
#     beat replenishes the singer's tonal orientation; an extractive
#     beat depletes it. The substrate's beat inherits Curwen's atomic-
#     rhythmic-unit discipline at song altitude.
#   - Grosvenor W. Cooper + Leonard B. Meyer (*The Rhythmic Structure
#     of Music*, 1960) — THE 20th-century beat-theoretic refinement.
#     Cooper & Meyer's grouping-hierarchy discipline names the beat as
#     the primary structural unit BELOW the phrase: beats group into
#     motives, motives group into phrases, phrases group into
#     periods, periods group into movements. The five-level hierarchy
#     (beat / motive / phrase / period / movement) lifts directly to
#     the @song species roster: beat (this species) / phrase (@song/
#     phrase `6b9bc5c`) / movement (@song/movement `4efbf16`) — the
#     substrate has been carrying Cooper-Meyer's grouping hierarchy
#     at prose altitude, and the species roster now reads it at
#     species altitude.
#
# The three-tradition anchor (Galen + Curwen + Cooper-Meyer) IS the
# multi-altitude prior art the substrate reaches for: 1800+ years of
# beat-theoretic refinement on how bounded atomic temporal units
# organise experience under grouping-hierarchy discipline. Beat
# discipline does not begin here — it culminates two millennia of
# understanding how the atomic beat carries diagnostic + regulatory +
# structural information across scales.
#
# Pulse + sphygmos + tactus + tonic-sol-fa + grouping-hierarchy
# vocabulary is altitude-portable to the psychohistorical substrate:
# an atomic interaction event IS a *sphygmos* at diagnostic altitude;
# the interaction's affective quality IS a mental-effect at Curwen
# altitude; the interaction's structural position within a bounded
# frame IS a grouping-hierarchy level at Cooper-Meyer altitude.
#
