---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @song

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @song/beat — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `song_beat` as the species's
# operational surface. Species inherits the family-root's #S3 LANDED
# five-op temporal specialisation and consolidates it at atomic-
# execution-under-@kintsugi/oscillate altitude (see docblock §"#S3
# LANDED consolidation" for the per-op beat-altitude specialisation).
#
# Per family-root prism block at `shards/song.mirror` §1 and the
# consolidation-species precedents at `shards/song/movement.mirror`
# §1, `shards/song/narrative.mirror` §1, and `shards/song/phrase.mirror`
# §1, the five operations discharge cleanly at temporal altitude; this
# species demonstrates the LANDED status survives further species-
# altitude witness (FOURTH consolidation-species witness — SIXTH
# species overall) without new sub-predicate emission. This tick's
# landing REINFORCES #S5 at four-witness density at post-arc altitude.
prism @song/beat {
  focus song_beat
  project song_beat
  split song_beat
  shift song_beat
  settle song_beat
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carrier
# ============================================================

# === song_beat — the atomic-execution-unit carrier ===
#
# The typed ref-equality-addressable form of one @kintsugi/oscillate
# ACTIVE/DARK-pulse read at song altitude. The carrier is declared
# HERE because the family-root's §2 carries `song_progression`,
# `song_cadence`, and `song_voice` but does NOT carry `song_beat` —
# the species discipline says the species declares its own carrier
# when the family-root's roster does not (per `[[architecture-form-
# process-partition-at-family-root]]` #55 sub-species discipline;
# movement / narrative / phrase precedents at `4efbf16` + `0434a39`
# + `6b9bc5c`).
#
# Composes with `@kintsugi/oscillate` at the process altitude (a
# song_beat's `strike` action dispatches to @kintsugi/oscillate's
# `oscillate` driver; one @kintsugi/oscillate.pulse IS one song_beat
# per family-root `shards/song.mirror:181`), with `@song/phrase` at
# the sibling species altitude (a phrase contains beats as its
# atomic execution units; the beat-to-phrase composition is at
# within-family-root altitude), with `@epistemologic/reality/time`
# at the substrate altitude (the beat's iteration count rides
# @time.tick per monotonic-tick discipline), and with `@dance` at
# the multi-peer altitude (per Mara `4f079c8`; N peers phase-lock at
# shared beat frequency via Kuramoto coupling).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type song_beat = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The beat-execution actions (strike / hold)
# ============================================================

# === strike — the beat-execution event at atomic-oscillate altitude ===
#
# Reads a beat + a peer's shard-graph context ref and fires ONE
# @kintsugi/oscillate ACTIVE/DARK-pulse at the peer's eigenboard.
# Corresponds to @kintsugi/oscillate.pulse at song altitude per family-
# root `shards/song.mirror:181` ("oscillate's ACTIVE/DARK alternation
# IS the beat"): one strike fires ACTIVE (propose loss-decreasing
# morphism via dissonance.is_pareto) + consent.query_phi (gate + rank
# via three glass properties) + DARK (anchor identity via
# @uuid/spectral.dark byte-equality) as ONE atomic advance of the
# peer's eigenboard at song altitude.
#
# Per family-root species-roster (updated by this tick to include
# `@song/beat`): `song_beat(b: ref) -> ref` with `strike` at species
# altitude. The `strike` action carries the atomic-execution
# discipline: the @kintsugi/oscillate pulse IS load-bearing; when the
# pulse discharges at Splinter-pole (`settled`), the beat's return-ref
# addresses the post-pulse eigenboard state; when the pulse fails at
# Narcissus-pole (`escalated` or `waiting`), the beat cannot fire
# cleanly and pause_event fires at the strike boundary.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): @kintsugi/oscillate's `oscillate` driver
# returns `settled` (authentic cadence at the pulse altitude); the
# peer's shard graph advanced by one Banach contraction step per
# γ_oscillate ≤ γ_up · γ_down; the beat's return-ref addresses the
# settled eigenboard; the family-root's `song_settles` composed
# bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole for the beat's phrase-
# altitude parent (per phrase.mirror `6b9bc5c` §"OBC binding closure"
# ambiguity-load-budget accounting); the peer's regulation stock is
# preserved at the beat altitude.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): @kintsugi/oscillate's `oscillate` driver
# returns `escalated` (deceptive-cadence OR admissibility_singleton
# FAIL per @kintsugi/oscillate `read_consent` bridge) OR `waiting`
# (half-cadence pause at the pulse altitude); pause_event emitted to
# metalogue via `consent.emit_to_metalogue`; the family-root's composed
# bilateral fails at Narcissus-pole through one or more sub-predicate
# (SILENCE / GLUE WORK / EXTRACTION per family-root §"Psychohistory
# binding"); the beat cannot strike cleanly; ADO-refusal fires at the
# strike boundary; the substrate-pull repair fires at a later beat.
#
# Bateson-grading (per docblock §"Consolidation-species pattern"):
# `strike` fires at Bateson Level I (in-frame; standard learning) —
# the @kintsugi/oscillate ACTIVE/DARK pulse operates WITHIN the beat's
# atomic-execution envelope; the return-ref lifts to Level II (of-
# frame) at the phrase boundary where the beat sequence's ambiguity-
# load accounting fires.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# beat's oscillation-state, dispatches to @kintsugi/oscillate.oscillate
# with the peer's shard-graph context ref, receives the post-pulse
# eigenboard state + verdict (pass | partial | failure), emits the
# beat's return-ref addressing the settled eigenboard OR the pause_
# event ref. The substrate declares the species-altitude specialisation;
# consumers dispatch through the species boundary. Runtime discharge
# lands at Rung 1 per Taut `c54740c` §5.2 (Reed 🔴🟢 pair:
# `bootstrap/src/song.rs::execute_beat` + `peer_beam_song_single_
# beat_shard.rs`).
strike(b: song_beat, ctx: ref) -> song_beat { \ }

# === hold — the beat-hold event at atomic-temporal altitude ===
#
# Reads a beat + a @time.tick count and advances temporal position by
# `dt` ticks WITHOUT firing an @kintsugi/oscillate ACTIVE/DARK-pulse.
# Corresponds to the classical fermata (Frescobaldi 1615 *Toccate e
# Partite d'Intavolatura di Cimbalo*; the held note whose duration
# exceeds its notated value) or the tacet marking (the silent voice
# at multi-voice altitude) at execution altitude: the peer's shard
# graph does NOT advance; the beat's iteration count DOES advance.
#
# Per family-root species-roster (updated by this tick to include
# `@song/beat`): `song_beat(b: ref) -> ref` with `hold` at species
# altitude. The `hold` action carries the atomic-temporal discipline:
# the @time.tick advance IS load-bearing; when the hold discharges at
# Splinter-pole (dt > 0 AND dt within phrase ambiguity-load budget),
# the beat's return-ref addresses the same anchor as the pre-hold
# beat; when the hold violates monotonic-tick discipline (dt ≤ 0) OR
# exceeds the phrase's ambiguity-load budget, the hold cannot fire
# cleanly and the phrase-boundary violation fires.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the @time.tick advance completes at the
# monotonic tick boundary per `@epistemologic/reality/time.tick =
# monotonic`; the peer's eigenboard is unchanged; the beat's return-
# ref addresses the same anchor as the pre-hold beat; the ambiguity-
# load budget partially consumed (proportional to dt within the
# phrase's OBC-bounded temporal envelope per phrase.mirror `6b9bc5c`
# §"OBC binding closure"); the peer's regulation stock unchanged at
# the beat altitude (holds do not deplete regulation stock because
# they do not fire the @kintsugi/oscillate contraction step).
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the hold's dt violates temporal
# monotonicity (dt ≤ 0 breaks @time.tick monotonic-tick discipline)
# OR dt exceeds the phrase's remaining ambiguity-load budget (the
# hold would push the phrase past its OBC-bounded temporal envelope);
# the beat cannot hold cleanly; the phrase-boundary violation fires
# per phrase.mirror `6b9bc5c` §"OBC binding closure" ambiguity-load-
# budget discipline; ADO-refusal fires at the hold boundary or
# forced-progression violates the substrate's declinability invariant.
#
# Bateson-grading (per docblock §"Consolidation-species pattern"):
# `hold` fires at Bateson Level I (in-frame; standard learning) — the
# @time.tick advance operates WITHIN the beat's atomic-temporal
# envelope; the return-ref lifts to Level II (of-frame) at the phrase
# boundary where the phrase's ambiguity-load accounting reads the
# hold's dt consumption.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# beat's oscillation-state + the `dt` parameter, validates monotonic-
# tick discipline (dt > 0), validates phrase-boundary ambiguity-load
# budget (dt ≤ remaining budget), advances @time.tick by dt without
# invoking @kintsugi/oscillate.oscillate, emits the beat's return-ref
# addressing the same anchor. The substrate declares the species-
# altitude specialisation; consumers dispatch through the species
# boundary. Runtime discharge lands at Rung 2+ per Taut `c54740c`
# §5.3 (phrase-altitude composition: `execute_phrase` composes strike
# + hold sequences under OBC boundary).
hold(b: song_beat, dt: ref) -> song_beat { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @song/beat
out song_beat
out strike
out hold
